{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train","id":831460,"title":"\u200bAll aboard the Dragon-Blooded Hype Train!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-16T20:43:30-08:00","id":831460,"title":"\u200bAll aboard the Dragon-Blooded Hype Train!","content":"So the Dragon-Blooded book is being drafted up and considering that the core is really good I am excited. As a person who never actually got to play exalted but twice (both solars) in second edition I never got to experience the joys and wonders of the Dragon Blooded. However I always thought that they had a lot of cool things going for them and now that I have a gaming group more interested in exalted games I look forward to the chance to actually get to play one.<br /> <br /> So what do you all think is going to be in the book? What are you hoping to see in the Dragon-Blooded book?<br /> <br /> It is going to be interesting to see the Dragon Blooded book because it is going to give us a clear idea of how the mechanics look from a different angle both from power and theme. Things I am hoping for include: New Spells (pretty much a given), the elemental styles, an idea of how evocations work for other exalts, and additional antagonists as well as more demons and elementals for summoners. Something I would really like is some focus on other Dragon blooded other than the Dynasts and Lookshy. I know they will make up the bulk of the book but I would be delighted for more information on Prasad, forest witches, the blood-bats, and some new groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T20:59:15-08:00","id":831472,"title":"","content":"Who are the Bloodbats?<br /> <br /> I am really looking forward to how they theme some powers like Martial arts to replicate Bending, and the greater detail on the Great Houses that supposedly will make them feel more like choosing a Clan in Vampire. And all the snippets on non Dynast Dragons! Yum!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T21:21:53-08:00","id":831487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831472#post831472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who are the Bloodbats?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are beastmen in the eastern wyld. They have a ruling council of dragon-blooded. They look like stereotypical bad guys but I think with some more attention they could be turned from a one note group of villains into a interesting character choice. They are the only dragon-blooded beastmen I know of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","user":"Snakesandsuns","date":". 02-17-2016, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T21:26:19-08:00","id":831490,"title":"","content":"When and where did we hear aboot this Fellas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T21:29:48-08:00","id":831491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831490#post831490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When and where did we hear aboot this Fellas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 123-124 in the Compass of Celestial Directions: The Wyld","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T21:52:25-08:00","id":831499,"title":"","content":"For me, how the Dragon Blooded are handled is going to be what makes or breaks this edition for me. This is partly because I am an unabashed Dragon Blooded fanboy and partly because this is when we're going to get to see if mixed exalt parties, the new combat system, evocations, and other stuff actually works for splats besides the solars. Also, it is when we will get to see if the fluff is going to be another Solar wankfest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T21:59:54-08:00","id":831501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831472#post831472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am really looking forward to how they theme some powers like Martial arts to replicate Bending</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get your hopes up. The devs have been pretty vocal about DBs not being benders, if anything they'll be deliberately avoiding making anything that replicates bending.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T22:21:21-08:00","id":831509,"title":"","content":"Ah I see. Well then I want to see how Elemental martial arts look in 3rd ed. And I want to see how well you can play a Dragonblooded who uses only one element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T22:36:07-08:00","id":831513,"title":"","content":"I dunno about bending specifically, but I'm really hoping for strong elemental themes. It's really lame if a Lunar who knows Air Dragon Style is more air-y than an Air Aspect who doesn't.<br /> <br /> And there's a lot of great design space in elemental themes. A lot of great design space that's not &quot;like Solars, but way worse&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T22:58:24-08:00","id":831519,"title":"","content":"I'd like the Dragon Blooded charms to be somewhat what they alluded to in the kickstarter sample.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">House Magic</span><br /> The point of saying certain Charms come from certain households has appeal to me. It almost feels a bit Legend of the 5 Rings where each of the Clans (7? 9? can't recall right now) each were thematically different but still had plenty of common ground. It also would lend a degree of history to a character which I have found players do like a lot in Exalted - knowing where their character has come from really makes their character pop from 2D cardboard into 3D fleshed out characters.<br /> <br /> From that I could see:<br /> - Iselsi playing the role of the &quot;Scorpion&quot;/ League of Shadows with an assortment of Stealth and Awareness techniques <br /> - Sesus playing the role of &quot;Theives guild&quot; with some tasty Larceny tricks<br /> - Tepet playing the roles of the &quot;Lion&quot; in devoting themselves to Warfare and squad tactics<br /> - Cathak being performers, presenters, and master duelists to promote their &quot;Heroes&quot;<br /> - Peleps/ V'Neef being the Sail masters/ Pirates<br /> <br /> And so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Elemental Effects</span><br /> Alternatively, seeing how they did Martial Arts with Terrestrial and Celestial levels, I could imagine they could do something similiar here (e.g.: certain Charms gain a boost if you are the Aspect type of that Charm's mechanic - so, as an example, any Dragon can learn Melee Charms to swing a sword at superhuman degrees but Firebloods will be able to add extra damage to their blade as it ignites the air).<br /> <br /> This could make for some interesting Charm divides too. Athletics (Jumping) would likely benefit from being Air-Aspected, while Athletics (Strength) may benefit from being Earth Aspected.<br /> <br /> I could see even a terrestrial equivilent (e.g.: Dragon Dodge charms are standard, but suffer a minor penalty if the practicioner is Earth or Wood blooded to suggest the etheral effect of Air, Water, and Flame).<br /> <br /> Personally I prefer this second path to the first, as it lends similar to the Solars (e.g.: Firebloods and Dawn are Melee Masters, Airbloods and Zenith are Beurocratic savants, Woodbloods and Twilights are prodigal doctors, etc...) but that's just me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the end I'll be satisfied if they make sure the Legacy of a Dragonblood to their family (or even lack of one in the case of a Lost Egg) plays a big part in their design. If the Solars are Sun Incarnate, the Abyssals are Death Incarnate, the Infernals are Hell Incarnate, etc... then the Dragons should be Legacy Incarnate. Family and ancestoral history should play a notable role in their theme because they differ from all other Exalts in their creation (aka they are bred; not so much chosen).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T23:10:29-08:00","id":831524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831513#post831513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's a lot of great design space in elemental themes. A lot of great design space that's not &quot;like Solars, but way worse&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>At first, I was just tempted to stalk this thread, like all the posts wishing DBs could be more Benderey, and call it a day. But this line in particular needed a call-out.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I'm most excited to see Evocation mechanics, the five Dragon Styles, and what (if any) Charms DBs have to help them work together as a group in combat. I am expecting to run Celestial-level games, so the makings of interesting antagonists are the most useful thing to me, mechanically.<br /> <br /> (Lore-wise, I am not sure how much will be in What Fire Has Wrought, which I am certainly buying, and the Realm setting book, which I am likely not. The notion of each Great House being designed to spur player loyalty like a Vampire Clan strikes me as intriguing-yet-misguided in any case.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T23:17:19-08:00","id":831525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831509#post831509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah I see. Well then I want to see how Elemental martial arts look in 3rd ed. And I want to see how well you can play a Dragonblooded who uses only one element.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that point, I'd certainly be curious to see at least 2 elemental styles for each element. Such as a Hard and Soft style suggestive of each &quot;Force&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... brainstorming ideas:<br /> <br /> Air<ul><li>Silent Void Style (absence of Air hides screams)</li> <li>Howling Breath Style (abundance of Air throws enemies asunder)</li> </ul><br /> Earth<ul><li>Steadfast Stone Style (solid and resilient; yet explosive like an Avalanche)</li> <li>Mercurial Heart Style (shifting and deceptive, yet sharp and savage when opportunity arrises)</li> </ul><br /> Fire<ul><li>Simmering Soul Style (calm and steady, warm and consistant, burning enemies over time)</li> <li>Explosive Rage Style (fast and reckless, end fights fast with overwhelming force before your own fuel is burned)</li> </ul><br /> Water<ul><li>Elusive Current Style (soft, smooth, elegent, relaxed. Able to move with incredible grace... or drunken unpredictability)</li> <li>Unbroken Glacier Style (similar to Steadfast stone; yet instead of being explosive in their attack they wear their foes down, slowing movements into submission)</li> </ul><br /> Wood<ul><li>Firm Oak (similar again to Steadfast Stone and Unbroken Glacier - a mid ground between explosive finishes and fights of attrition. Balanced and constant)</li> <li>Whispering Vine (almost a hybrid of Crane and Snake - evasive but with deadly, swift, and venomous counter-strikes)</li> </ul><br /> Alternatively I could see some similar styles being merged with only cosmetic differences. Steadfast Stone, Unbroken Glacier, and Firm Oak could all be a single style that benefit slightly when practiced by these three elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T23:20:15-08:00","id":831526,"title":"","content":"Well DBs were one of my favourite splats in second edition because they were a lot easier to tone back and not run absolutely roughshod all over everything else in the setting. It was pretty cool to actually have to work together to overcome challenges that weren't battles with yozi. On the flip side though, third edition had been doing a pretty good job of making Solars feel like that, and I think it's going to be really jarring to go to DBs after that.<br /> <br /> Theyre not getting supernal or anything like supernal, obviously, they might not get solar XP, and if it's like second Ed they'll get less attributes and charms with higher XP and BP costs and a slower essence advancement track. Combo that with smaller mote pools, dice caps, less efficient and weaker charms....it might suck.<br /> <br /> I'm glad they don't get supernal, I'm not sure they should have a solar-XP alike because solar XP was to solve a problem that DBs never had. Less attributes and charms, and slower essence progression, okay, but I think maybe it should stop there. Adding extra XP and BP costs onto that feels excessive. Playing a DB is supposed to feel kind of weak and restrictive, it's why every aspect has their role and really strong incentives not to stray from that role, but it can be a bit much.<br /> <br /> Also super doubtful there's going to be new antagonists and demons and spells and stuff, those usually show up in their own books. The Realm setting book will probably have a few though. <br /> <br /> <br /> What I'm excited to see are the changes they're making to the houses though. Those sound pretty cool. I'm also mega curious about how they're going to do the dragon styles and if they have the mastery keyword or not. There's really good reasons to have it and also good ones to not.<br /> <br /> Edit: also I'm with kejak, even the players in my group who didn't like Solars before love them now, so I'm betting strongly on DBs being more antagonists than players, and I really want strong teamwork tactics since being the ST lets me essentially craft whole sworn brotherhoods as units.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 02-17-2016, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T23:33:53-08:00","id":831533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831519#post831519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">House Magic</span><br /> The point of saying certain Charms come from certain households has appeal to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I like that idea too. Gonna be tricky to balance, though.<br /> <br /> A side benefit that just occurred to me: if certain Charms are for certain bloodlines, it provides a natural thing for the Breeding Merit to do. One that's interesting and worth buying, but not mandatory for everyone who cares about optimization.<br /> <br /> (I like this idea partially because it means that Breeding can actually improve over generations through House-founding and legacy-building. Never been keen on the whole &quot;our power is forever dwindling because we compromised our racial/species/whatever purity&quot; thing.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831519#post831519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...any Dragon can learn Melee Charms to swing a sword at superhuman degrees but Firebloods will be able to add extra damage to their blade as it ignites the air).<br /> <br /> This could make for some interesting Charm divides too. Athletics (Jumping) would likely benefit from being Air-Aspected, while Athletics (Strength) may benefit from being Earth Aspected.<br /> <br /> I could see even a terrestrial equivilent (e.g.: Dragon Dodge charms are standard, but suffer a minor penalty if the practicioner is Earth or Wood blooded to suggest the etheral effect of Air, Water, and Flame).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping they don't couple abilities too tightly to Aspects. A Melee Charm that's got a special bonus for Fire Aspects is cool, but so is one that's got a special bonus for Wood Aspects. &quot;Melee&quot; isn't really a thing in setting, and there's no reason to say fighting with a wooden club isn't a Wood Aspect thing just because Melee is listed as a Fire Ability.<br /> <br /> If most of Melee is Fire, most of Resistance is Earth, and so on, that's fine. But I think there should be at least a bit of wiggle room.<br /> <br /> The preview PDF is very encouraging on this score. They've been known to change their minds, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831524#post831524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Lore-wise, I am not sure how much will be in What Fire Has Wrought, which I am certainly buying, and the Realm setting book, which I am likely not. The notion of each Great House being designed to spur player loyalty like a Vampire Clan strikes me as intriguing-yet-misguided in any case.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why misguided?<br /> <br /> It sounds like a good idea to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T04:05:31-08:00","id":831641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">what do you all think is going to be in the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I'm honestly not sure. I mean, the Realm book is coming out around the same time, and apparently that's going to be the one with a lot of the Dynasty stuff, which always formed a major bulk of Dragon Blooded books... I wonder if, rather than a specific breakdown of the Dynasty or the Shogunate, there'll be a myth and history section that gets into the broad strokes of how and why they keep establishing military governments.<br /> <br /> Probably also some stuff on that pilgrimage route on the Caul.<br /> <br /> Other than that... I wonder if the premise of a greatly expanded Charm set might entail somewhat briefer setting details, especially when the Realm book is coming on the heels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you hoping to see in the Dragon-Blooded book?</div> </div> </div> </div>A follow up to that suggestion of a greatly simplified Breeding Merit, I suppose. Also, fewer Charms that are so fixated on a &quot;by your powers combined&quot; angle. Eh, I'm mostly willing to take what is placed before me rather than set my own standards.<br /> <br /> I believe people should know that, at the most recent statement that I ever saw, they said that they found the whole House-specific Charms thing to be too wonky in implementation, so they shifted the emphasis to distinct Evocations of legacy weapons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this idea partially because it means that Breeding can actually improve over generations through House-founding and legacy-building. Never been keen on the whole &quot;our power is forever dwindling because we compromised our racial/species/whatever purity&quot; thing</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree. Indeed, it's my personal view that the best bred scions of the Scarlet Dynasty are better than basically anybody from the First Age or Shogunate, on account of it not really being necessary to have increased numbers of magical children when there are hundreds of thousands of them.<br /> <br /> Also the idea that having children with a well-bred mortal is only slightly less effective than a well-bred Exalt, and far better than an outcaste. The idea of a Merit that mortals can buy is another positive to me. The whole thing would make me think that Terrestrial Exalted having mortal children has been a thing since about forever, and they were still good for arranged marriages (even if, a fair bit into the Old Realm, only to a particularly stingy group).<br /> <br /> The Dragon Blooded should be dwindling because things like ancient plague, Fair Folk, and Lunars keep killing them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T04:13:41-08:00","id":831645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831533#post831533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why misguided?<br /> <br /> It sounds like a good idea to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, he's Chejop Kejak - of course he doesn't want people to identify or sympathize with any DB socio-political structure, makes it harder for him to sacrifice them for the good of Creation later on! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T04:51:43-08:00","id":831660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831533#post831533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why misguided?<br /> <br /> It sounds like a good idea to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because approximately every game ever which has committed to this whole early White Wolf paradigm of &quot;the splats are explicitly written so that fans of one dislike all the others,&quot; from the oWoD itself to Legend of the Five Rings to Ninja Crusade, has accomplished the same thing: making it totally impossible to ever get a group of players to work together short of limiting their options at CharGen. And for Dragon-Bloods, traditionally the least mixed party-friendly Exalt type, limiting those options doesn't seem like a great call to me.<br /> <br /> It also further encourages people to view the Realm as interacting with itself, rather than with the Threshold, which troubles me, but I'm willing to believe that they'll manage to not make the Realm so stone boring this edition, so that will probably be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T04:58:43-08:00","id":831665,"title":"","content":"I played a ton of Dragonblood back in the day, far more than Celestial games. I got bored of them from over-use, but there was nothing fundamentally wrong with them, except a few badly written charms.*<br /> Which means there's nothing I'm particularly excited about it in this book. I'm nervous** but interested in what they do with the Houses. It might shake things up a bit: as I said, while I think the DBs and Dynasty were one of the best parts of the game, after playing about 7 Dragonblood characters I got bored of them, so changing things might reinvigorate my interest.<br /> In the game I run, I've had a reinvigorated Realm starting to reinvade the Realm a few decades after the canon start, so if I really like the Dragonblood book, I can make them the primary antagonists. I never used them much as antagonists in 2nd ed because I was bored of them.<br /> <br /> I guess the only thing I would like them to improve (and think they will) is the Blessed Isle itself. The Dynasty was interesting, but the Blessed Isle, as a peaceful but stratified society, was the most boring place in the entire setting. But a couple of the writers said they found the exact same thing, so I expect this to be a priority for the Realm book.<br /> <br /> *The interesting thing about the Dragonblood book is the way the charms were some of the most badly-written, probably second-worst after the Sidereals, and yet mechanically the Dragonblood probably worked better in 2e than any other splat, because their combats didn't consist of 15 paranoia-combos in a row followed by instant death.<br /> <br /> **I think most of the Houses were fine before. Sometimes people complain about the Houses on this forum for various reasons, but I tend to think they're the complaints of people who haven't read the books properly. So, I'm a little nervous about what they're going to do with the Houses: maybe they'll ruin them! But, generally I'm pretty happy with the fluff this team writes, so I'm not really that worried.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-17-2016, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T05:08:06-08:00","id":831672,"title":"","content":"I got into Legend of Five Rings recently and was struck by how much Rokugan resembles the Realm I want. With increased emphasis on distinct Houses, I am hoping the new DB books will deliver.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, I really hope there will be more support for non-Dynast Dragon-Bloods. DBs have the potential to be the most diverse splat aside from Solars and Exigents, and pigeonholing them only as aristocratic jerks is a waste of their potential.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831491#post831491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 123-124 in the Compass of Celestial Directions: The Wyld</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thank you! I <i>knew </i>I had seen canon beastmen Dragon-Bloods somewhere and I was going mad trying to figure out where.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 02-17-2016, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T06:42:25-08:00","id":831709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831672#post831672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from that, I really hope there will be more support for non-Dynast Dragon-Bloods. DBs have the potential to be the most diverse splat aside from Solars and Exigents, and pigeonholing them only as aristocratic jerks is a waste of their potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a thing that'd be nice to see, more cadet houses, small dynasties (like Kel Beraz... who is his family?), etc.<br /> <br /> Oh, and while it amused me, let's not having time-travelling impregnation again. I'm confident that the writers this time can remember when houses actually began.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T07:08:09-08:00","id":831720,"title":"","content":"Regarding expanding on the Houses and maybe giving them some truly unique things, my friend recently bought L5R 4e, and among many things he told me about the system, he said that multi-Clan teams are finally viable! I shrugged and told him they were always viable, you just had to apply a iota of common sense to clan writeups and understand they present trends and stereotypes rather than sum total of clan behavior.<br /> <br /> Seriously, all it takes is common sense. Granted, it's a quality suspiciously rare in RPG fandom, or at least its vocal part, but I've yet to see a system where the writing would be truly responsible for these kind of issues. In all cases I'm aware of, it's a failure of reading comprehension that causes them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T07:21:16-08:00","id":831728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train#post831460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...an idea of how evocations work for other exalts...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831499#post831499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...evocations...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831524#post831524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I'm most excited to see Evocation mechanics...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, for evocations at least, we're very likely to get information about Dragonblooded interactions 2 books earlier than What Fire Has Wrought. Supposedly all the rules for them should be in Arms of the Chosen.<br /> <br /> I know, everyone is SHOCKED that this is the one thing I contribute to this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T08:09:23-08:00","id":831744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">paradigm of &quot;the splats are explicitly written so that fans of one dislike all the others</div> </div> </div> </div> I really don't think that's the intention, and, to me, for one to read it into the idea of trying to make them as iconic as the Vampire Clans makes only slightly more sense than assuming that such would entail rewriting them to drink blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T08:26:02-08:00","id":831753,"title":"","content":"Wahooo! Hype Train!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://acidspiders.files.wordpress.com/2016/02/dragonbloodedhypetrain.jpg?w=656\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Yes, I know Dragonblooded aren't benders, but who cares!<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To be honest, I think the Dynast Houses are better than most RPG Noble Houses. The Pathfinder Brevoy Houses are really dull. &quot;Here is yet another Arrogant Noble house of merchants that sells&quot; *spins commodity wheel* &quot;Fish!&quot;<br /> <br /> I just really want to play Solars on the Blessed Isle without it being Total Suicide. Maybe have the actual Realm Civil War break out, instead of just impeding. A Dynast house would be willing to make a deal with the Anathema if they are desperate enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T08:32:36-08:00","id":831757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831753#post831753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe have the actual Realm Civil War break out, instead of just impeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually reminds me of something that was mentioned a year or two ago in the discussion of how the setting might end up being presented by the Devs. Rather, not specifically that the Civil War would be detailed, but that settings would be presented with a timeline. What the status-quo was like just prior to Year Zero (with Year Zero being when the Solars appear) or at Year Zero, just after Year Zero, and like 10 years later. So you'd see the potential progression of an area and how things will occur without your characters interacting with it. <br /> <br /> It was a neat idea and I'm curious to see if they stick with it, because things like the Realm Civil War would be detailed in this manner (or at least the progression towards it) and gives players a lot of plot hooks. You can see how things set up earlier can leave to certain outcomes unless YOU intervene. What this should NEVER include is what happens if you DO get involved. That's how you avoid RotSE. Player interaction should change the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T08:49:16-08:00","id":831770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831753#post831753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just really want to play Solars on the Blessed Isle without it being Total Suicide. Maybe have the actual Realm Civil War break out, instead of just impeding. A Dynast house would be willing to make a deal with the Anathema if they are desperate enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I identified a problem in my head thanks to this, so thank you.<br /> <br /> I react badly to the suggestion that some anathema gets to survive on the blessed isle, but that is because the DB lose everywhere. After year zero they just don't get to win so to me it feels like they should have at least one safe space.<br /> <br /> Essentially the narrative for the Realm needs to be that they can actually win and solve problems. Their place in the setting of the crumbling empire seems to only allow tragedies to be run, which is a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:00:00-08:00","id":831779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831770#post831770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I identified a problem in my head thanks to this, so thank you.<br /> <br /> I react badly to the suggestion that some anathema gets to survive on the blessed isle, but that is because the DB lose everywhere. After year zero they just don't get to win so to me it feels like they should have at least one safe space.<br /> <br /> Essentially the narrative for the Realm needs to be that they can actually win and solve problems. Their place in the setting of the crumbling empire seems to only allow tragedies to be run, which is a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think the problem is more &quot;Dragonblooded Lose Everywhere that isn't the Blessed Isle.&quot; I don't want &quot;Dragonblooded Win on the Blessed Isle. Solars Win in the Threshold.&quot; Having that as a predetermined outcome is boring. I want my PCs to have a chance to win, no matter if they are a Circle of Dynasts in the South or a Circle of Solars on the Blessed Isle.<br /> <br /> <br /> No Place should be considered &quot;Safe Place&quot; for a Splat. I want plot hooks for Sidereals to fight Geiman on the Streets of Yu-Shan. I want there to be Lunars infiltrating the Imperial Court. I want Solars causing chaos among the Terrestrial Gods.<br /> <br /> Now Dynasts should have a home field advantage on the Blessed Isle, but I want them to have trouble sleeping at night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-17-2016, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:01:53-08:00","id":831782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831501#post831501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't get your hopes up. The devs have been pretty vocal about DBs not being benders, if anything they'll be deliberately avoiding making anything that replicates bending.</div> </div> </div> </div>One Charm so far is a direct homage to something in Avatar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:03:32-08:00","id":831785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831770#post831770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I identified a problem in my head thanks to this, so thank you.<br /> <br /> I react badly to the suggestion that some anathema gets to survive on the blessed isle, but that is because the DB lose everywhere. After year zero they just don't get to win so to me it feels like they should have at least one safe space.<br /> <br /> Essentially the narrative for the Realm needs to be that they can actually win and solve problems. Their place in the setting of the crumbling empire seems to only allow tragedies to be run, which is a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what little we have on the Empire in this edition leans away from &quot;crumbling empire on the brink of dissolution&quot; and towards &quot;still Creation's biggest player, but held back by growing decadence, corruption and internal strife&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:11:04-08:00","id":831789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831779#post831779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I think the problem is more &quot;Dragonblooded Lose Everywhere that isn't the Blessed Isle.&quot; I don't want &quot;Dragonblooded Win on the Blessed Isle. Solars Win in the Threshold.&quot; Having that as a predetermined outcome is boring. I want my PCs to have a chance to win, no matter if they are a Circle of Dynasts in the South or a Circle of Solars on the Blessed Isle.<br /> <br /> <br /> No Place should be considered &quot;Safe Place&quot; for a Splat. I want plot hooks for Sidereals to fight Geiman on the Streets of Yu-Shan. I want there to be Lunars infiltrating the Imperial Court. I want Solars causing chaos among the Terrestrial Gods.<br /> <br /> Now Dynasts should have a home field advantage on the Blessed Isle, but I want them to have trouble sleeping at night.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, however with the setting the way it was left at the end of 2nd ed that wasn't the case. And then there was the problem that the mechanics didn't allow DB to win past a certain xp point, which meant that they stopped being good antagonists and the Realm just become a chew toy.<br /> <br /> So in short, the realm should be possible for solars/lunars etc, just not very easy and not for a starting celestial to piss all over and the same for DB and threshold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:15:42-08:00","id":831794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831782#post831782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Charm so far is a direct homage to something in Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Time to play &quot;Guess the Charm!&quot;<br /> <br /> Water Whip?<br /> Air Scooter?<br /> Channel Lightning Strikes?<br /> <br /> We already have Toph's &quot;Sense Vibrations though the Earth&quot; with Awareness Charms. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:20:26-08:00","id":831801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831794#post831794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Time to play &quot;Guess the Charm!&quot;<br /> <br /> Water Whip?<br /> Air Scooter?<br /> Channel Lightning Strikes?<br /> <br /> We already have Toph's &quot;Sense Vibrations though the Earth&quot; with Awareness Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Water Octopus form, imo","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:22:23-08:00","id":831804,"title":"","content":"Speaking of DB hype, I read Houses of the Bull God recently, and I'm itching to run a game about a group of young Dragon-Blooded arriving in Harborhead for luxury vacation after their graduation... right before shit hits the fan and the whole province rises up against its oppressors.<br /> <br /> Seriously, if What Fire Has Wrought came out yesterday, it wouldn't be soon enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:26:47-08:00","id":831808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831789#post831789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are right, however with the setting the way it was left at the end of 2nd ed that wasn't the case. And then there was the problem that the mechanics didn't allow DB to win past a certain xp point, which meant that they stopped being good antagonists and the Realm just become a chew toy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You have to be careful not to get too in &quot;But that splat was shit in 2nd Edition!&quot; I've been down that rabbit hole many times with Sidereals and it isn't a pleasant place. I'm trying to be hopefully optimistic about Ex3 Dragonblooded and Sidereals and reserving judgement until the books come out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831789#post831789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in short, the realm should be possible for solars/lunars etc, just not very easy and not for a starting celestial to piss all over and the same for DB and threshold.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I want a challenge for Solars. There has to be a happy medium between Bronze Faction Hit Squads breaking down doors of careful and stealthy Solars and Anathema flaring Anima in the middle of the Imperial Court and getting away with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-17-2016, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:26:47-08:00","id":831809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831782#post831782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Charm so far is a direct homage to something in Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Intriguing!<br /> <br /> I was going to make a joke about the Charm just being something trivial and non-Bendey, such as Cabbage-Crushing Cart Correction, but since tone is so difficult to assess, in text, I feel I ought to be clear in saying that I am genuinely pleased by this news, and eager to see what Charm(s) Robert means.<br /> <br /> Besides, CCCC woulda been <i>so</i> broken. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:30:29-08:00","id":831811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831809#post831809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Intriguing!<br /> <br /> I was going to make a joke about the Charm just being something trivial and non-Bendey, such as Cabbage-Crushing Cart Correction, but since tone is so difficult to assess, in text, I feel I ought to be clear in saying that I am genuinely pleased by this news, and eager to see what Charm(s) Robert means.<br /> <br /> Besides, CCCC woulda been <i>so</i> broken. :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cabbage-Crushing Cart Correction is the counter-charm to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/782476-ex3-sidereal-update-homebrew?p=787604#post787604\">Pho Cart Methodology</a>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:31:04-08:00","id":831812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831809#post831809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Intriguing!<br /> <br /> I was going to make a joke about the Charm just being something trivial and non-Bendey, such as Cabbage-Crushing Cart Correction, but since tone is so difficult to assess, in text, I feel I ought to be clear in saying that I am genuinely pleased by this news, and eager to see what Charm(s) Robert means.<br /> <br /> Besides, CCCC woulda been <i>so</i> broken. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solar party in response:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m8ko3dHPqL1qd9kcuo2_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:31:32-08:00","id":831814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831782#post831782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Charm so far is a direct homage to something in Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to bet on Toph Sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T11:25:43-08:00","id":831902,"title":"","content":"Toph sense has been a thing for a while, though. It's like the only reason Awareness is Earth aspected. So if it is just Toph Sense I'll be pretty disappointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T11:30:23-08:00","id":831913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train#post831460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Dragon-Blooded book is being drafted up and considering that the core is really good I am excited. As a person who never actually got to play exalted but twice (both solars) in second edition I never got to experience the joys and wonders of the Dragon Blooded. However I always thought that they had a lot of cool things going for them and now that I have a gaming group more interested in exalted games I look forward to the chance to actually get to play one.<br /> <br /> So what do you all think is going to be in the book? What are you hoping to see in the Dragon-Blooded book?<br /> <br /> It is going to be interesting to see the Dragon Blooded book because it is going to give us a clear idea of how the mechanics look from a different angle both from power and theme. Things I am hoping for include: New Spells (pretty much a given), the elemental styles, an idea of how evocations work for other exalts, and additional antagonists as well as more demons and elementals for summoners. Something I would really like is some focus on other Dragon blooded other than the Dynasts and Lookshy. I know they will make up the bulk of the book but I would be delighted for more information on Prasad, forest witches, the blood-bats, and some new groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am looking forward to an immense joy of mine. Playing the outcaste DB who somehow gets more done than all the solars and celestials in the group. <br /> <br /> I am looking forward to storied lineages and storied items of inheritance. I am looking forward to a robust charmset where I can feel like I can make an air aspect swordsman who doesn't get shot in the foot every time they activate Dragon Graced Weapon. I am looking forward to seeing the immaculate styles. (would really hope that becomes one of those things where its better for a DB than for another exalt). <br /> <br /> Looking forward to playing my immaculate Little Mountain and my thief Slip.<br /> <br /> They are my favorite splat, I love the whole Romance of Three Kingdoms feel they have. I want that game. I want it so bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T11:58:20-08:00","id":831939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831794#post831794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Time to play &quot;Guess the Charm!&quot;<br /> <br /> Water Whip?<br /> Air Scooter?<br /> Channel Lightning Strikes?<br /> <br /> We already have Toph's &quot;Sense Vibrations though the Earth&quot; with Awareness Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm putting my bet on Platypus-Bear Combination. Something that goes of Hybrid Body Rearrangement and lets you mix two heartsblood forms. I actually wrote up the charm but the forum ate it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831808#post831808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You have to be careful not to get too in &quot;But that splat was shit in 2nd Edition!&quot; I've been down that rabbit hole many times with Sidereals and it isn't a pleasant place. I'm trying to be hopefully optimistic about Ex3 Dragonblooded and Sidereals and reserving judgement until the books come out.<br /> <br /> This. I want a challenge for Solars. There has to be a happy medium between Bronze Faction Hit Squads breaking down doors of careful and stealthy Solars and Anathema flaring Anima in the middle of the Imperial Court and getting away with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to be fair, with great effort and leveraging a ton of power from the Empire it is actually possible to challenge Solars in this edition with the Scarlet empire. At least I think so, I actually haven't tried yet but I'm hoping.<br /> <br /> The problem is that all the fiction about DBs paints them in a pretty...stormtrooper light a lot of the time. Actually, somewhat worse than that considering Force Awakens now.<br /> <br /> Spoilers for Force Awakens<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Okay, so you know that scene that the movie opens up with, when the stormtroopers bust down into that kind of rebel village and just kill everyone, and then Kylo Ren shows up, kills the main guy and takes Poe prisoner? I think the Realm/DB book needs a scene like that, somewhere where a lot of brave people just get crushed by the overwhelming power of the Empire.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Also I could do with a scene where a dude who knows every single DB brawl charm has an epic fistfight with a Bloodape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 02-17-2016, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:02:34-08:00","id":831943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831782#post831782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Charm so far is a direct homage to something in Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're hoping it's a cool bending power, but it's really...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/8BjH7M9.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:09:20-08:00","id":831952,"title":"","content":"You know, this thread reminds me of something that caught my eye in the backer pdf regarding the Immaculate Styles:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex3 p.72</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The power of Terrestrial Exalted who undergo the Order\u2019s martial art training is beyond question. Immaculates spend their lives developing their Essence, and <b>use the natural Charms of their kind mixed freely with the proprietary Immaculate martial arts styles </b>to perform feats of martial prowess notable even among the Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. This could admittedly mean absolutely nothing (Solars mix their Charms with Martial Arts too if you count supplementing your combat suite with Dodge, Resistance, Athletics, Awareness and such), but it could also mean the Dragon-Blooded can use their native combat abilities alongside Immaculate Styles in a way other Exalts can't, like supplementing a shortsword attack with both Fire Dragon and Terrestrial Melee Charms. That'd be pretty cool, don't you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:09:48-08:00","id":831954,"title":"","content":"As a resident not fan of Dragonblooded. Mostly I am hoping that the House intrigues and expansions of the Houses lives up to the hype and that their mechanics are solid and enjoyable for both DB fans and those who mostly use them as NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T12:20:24-08:00","id":831963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831952#post831952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...it could also mean the Dragon-Blooded can use their native combat abilities alongside Immaculate Styles in a way other Exalts can't, like supplementing a shortsword attack with both Fire Dragon and Terrestrial Melee Charms. That'd be pretty cool, don't you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a great catch and a fascinating proposition. That WOULD certainly change the story for DBs.<br /> <br /> My impression between the backer PDF and Dev forum commentary was that DBs would get Martial Arts with the Terrestrial keyword, and then if they initiated to Immaculate level, they would get to ignore that keyword (and be on par with Lunars and such) but lack the Mastery keyword still. But getting to mix in native combat charms would definitely change the game! Now I'm hoping that's the case!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T14:21:47-08:00","id":832069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831963#post831963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is a great catch and a fascinating proposition. That WOULD certainly change the story for DBs.<br /> <br /> My impression between the backer PDF and Dev forum commentary was that DBs would get Martial Arts with the Terrestrial keyword, and then if they initiated to Immaculate level, they would get to ignore that keyword (and be on par with Lunars and such) but lack the Mastery keyword still. But getting to mix in native combat charms would definitely change the game! Now I'm hoping that's the case!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure that would be a good thing. It's certainly possible, but then the Dragon styles would have to be balanced around the fact that you can do a fire dragon strike AND enhance it with Dragon Graced Weapon. Which basically means that the Dragon styles would all have to be really crappy. If anything I think it would be cooler if they stipulated that charms from the Immaculate styles couldn't be combined with any charms outside their style, not even other martial arts, and then let them be good and solid on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T14:41:02-08:00","id":832082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831963#post831963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> My impression between the backer PDF and Dev forum commentary was that DBs would get Martial Arts with the Terrestrial keyword, and then if they initiated to Immaculate level, they would get to ignore that keyword (and be on par with Lunars and such) but lack the Mastery keyword still.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking it could be this, plus maybe for the Immaculate styles, they in fact DO get the mastery keyword, hence the idea that those styles in particular are somehow more spiritually powerful or sacred.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1398-corwin859","name":"corwin859","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T14:42:18-08:00","id":832084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TDS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831902#post831902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Toph sense has been a thing for a while, though. It's like the only reason Awareness is Earth aspected. So if it is just Toph Sense I'll be pretty disappointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting enough, <b>Exalted: the Dragon-Blooded</b> came out in April 2002 and <b>Aspect Book: Earth</b> in March 2004, a good two years before Toph ever premiered. The latter book even had a blind character who used Earth sense to navigate things and Charms for doing that.<br /> <br /> (Awareness actually is Earth probably because of Earth's general &quot;center&quot; Ability, if that makes any sense. Like Martial Arts being Earth originally for it being the ordered, disicplined Ability that fit katas and all that.)<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T14:50:05-08:00","id":832091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=832069#post832069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not so sure that would be a good thing. It's certainly possible, but then the Dragon styles would have to be balanced around the fact that you can do a fire dragon strike AND enhance it with Dragon Graced Weapon. Which basically means that the Dragon styles would all have to be really crappy. If anything I think it would be cooler if they stipulated that charms from the Immaculate styles couldn't be combined with any charms outside their style, not even other martial arts, and then let them be good and solid on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is counterintuitive to the point of sounding paranoid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T14:58:05-08:00","id":832098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=832091#post832091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is counterintuitive to the point of sounding paranoid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, Smouldering Wound Attack enhanced with Dragon Graced Weapon and Ringing Anvil Onslaught seems like it would get pretty ridiculous pretty fast. I think they should be allowed to be combined, kind of, but only if your earth aspect's tetsubo is being enhanced by the fire aspect swordsman who sets it aflame or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:13:50-08:00","id":832106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831782#post831782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Charm so far is a direct homage to something in Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to guess scarring someone/leaving a permanent mark as a show of disgrace.<br /> But I think that might be a Solar charm in the corebook now that I think about it, Hmmm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:17:14-08:00","id":832108,"title":"","content":"I did some thinking and Stormwind Rider is similar to Air Scooter, so it isn't that.<br /> <br /> Water Whip is still on the table. <br /> <br /> Though knowing our luck, the devs are trolling us:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://37.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_mczu0dlATZ1rjg0m8o1_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:19:57-08:00","id":832111,"title":"","content":"Martial Arts are quite powerful but limited to a particular strategy. Letting DBs combo them with their (weaker) native Charms would give them access to a more comprehensive combat suite that is nevertheless still not quite as good as a native combat Ability of a Celestial Exalt. This sounds about appropriate to how badass Immaculates are supposed to be, and is certainly a more interesting way of getting them to that level than what you propose, which would limit their mechanical options drastically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:20:22-08:00","id":832112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>corwin859</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=832082#post832082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking it could be this, plus maybe for the Immaculate styles, they in fact DO get the mastery keyword, hence the idea that those styles in particular are somehow more spiritually powerful or sacred.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this idea. Thematically, it justifies the in setting hype Immaculates receive; Mechanically, it makes mixed exalt parties or Solar hunter parties more viable and would fit well with them having Solar Tier Evocations within a limited purview (jade); and personally, I will just be kind of disappointed if the Immaculate styles can only be 'truly' mastered by non Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> If the devs don't give the Immaculates the mastery keyword, I may just houserule it in anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:47:42-08:00","id":832136,"title":"","content":"The purpose of Mastery keyword is to make MA viable for Solars (and give an edge to Sidereals). It makes no sense to offer the same bonus to Immaculates, who are already buying Charms stronger than their native suite when using non-Mastery, non-Terrestrial MA.<br /> <br /> (Cool as this new system is, the terminology of MA &quot;tiers&quot; doesn't exactly roll out of my tongue this time around. Can we agree to call MA used at default level &quot;Celestial&quot;? Then we'd have MA working at Terrestial, Celestial and Mastery levels from weakest to strongest, with Sidereal MA presumably being their own thing entirely.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:57:19-08:00","id":832145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831665#post831665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I played a ton of Dragonblood back in the day, far more than Celestial games. I got bored of them from over-use, but there was nothing fundamentally wrong with them, except a few badly written charms.*<br /> <br /> Which means there's nothing I'm particularly excited about it in this book. I'm nervous** but interested in what they do with the Houses. It might shake things up a bit: as I said, while I think the DBs and Dynasty were one of the best parts of the game, after playing about 7 Dragonblood characters I got bored of them, so changing things might reinvigorate my interest.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831665#post831665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the only thing I would like them to improve (and think they will) is the Blessed Isle itself. The Dynasty was interesting, but the Blessed Isle, as a peaceful but stratified society, was the most boring place in the entire setting. But a couple of the writers said they found the exact same thing, so I expect this to be a priority for the Realm book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like I agree with most of this. I want to be on the hype train but... really, the Dragonblooded are pretty well done as they are, so maybe just a little refocusing and some mix ups on the Houses to keep them fresh and get the ideas running would be cool. I'm not so totally into 3e's Realm compared to the previous editions, still keen to see what comes out of it.<br /> <br /> I want to note, internally peaceful societies really shouldn't be boring - in history the places like Tang Dynasty China or Edo Japan that had enough internal peace in which to develop the society were really the most interesting. They need social movements, cosmopolitanism and business life to actually be allowed to develop though. The Realm of the Scarlet Dynasty is perhaps more Ming than Tang or Song, I think (insularity, focused on an ideal of a society of peasant farmers?) still a lot should happen.<br /> <br /> For the Dragonblooded's Charms, I really feel like what I want to see is the authors really dig deep and come up with great heroic genre tricks which are achieved via or adapted to take into account elemental power (including powers like elemental bending). This is what feels to me what Dragonblooded Charms really ought to be. In the &quot;iconic Dragonblooded Charms&quot; thread, I thought there were some trees that really did this well, so that level of quality throughout the set and with more Charms, would be great. <br /> <br /> I actually also feel like a lot of the classic Dragonblooded Charms did a really good job of giving options and tools without automatically solving problems, particularly for social information and intrigue, which Dragonblooded should really be well set up for (if less well compared to Solars for actually revolutionizing societies or infiltrating their highest levels secretly or offsetting actually really really huge social disadvantages through charisma alone, etc). I'm sure when the writers look at them, they'll find them a good resource to update. But a lot of those could stand to be more &quot;elemental&quot; if it's possible.<br /> <br /> I'm really not too bothered about out of Aspect Ability Charms, like Air Resistance, Water Archery, etc. So long as whatever 3e's version of Out of Aspect charge isn't harsh, limiting and unfun. Dragonblooded Charms play a little looser with placement in some ways, so I'm happy with the summoning armour Air Charm being Thrown, not Resistance, etc. I also do view playing a Dragonblooded as, to a degree, playing a pan-elemental Exalt, and not just, the Exalt of Fire or Earth, who only acts through that channel. Obviously YMMV and there might be compelling game design reasons for another approach.<br /> <br /> Also +1 for Outcastes being great and being keen to see good stuff for them. Especially since the Realm is so mapped out, and there's so much space left in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:06:43-08:00","id":832153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=832106#post832106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going to guess scarring someone/leaving a permanent mark as a show of disgrace.<br /> But I think that might be a Solar charm in the corebook now that I think about it, Hmmm...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one of the sample Abyssal's charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:09:40-08:00","id":832154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=831779#post831779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want plot hooks for Sidereals to fight Geiman on the Streets of Yu-Shan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals vs. Neil Gaiman in an all-out celestial cage match to the death! Taking all bets!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:11:45-08:00","id":832155,"title":"","content":"It feels weird to imagine Mastery effects for Immaculate Styles which Immaculates do not get. I think if you did have to include them, then they should be styled in a way that's like &quot;Well, actually the Solar's *less* in connection with the style on an elemental level, as reflected in their mechanics, yet, they just punch really hard with it anyway, because Solar essence&quot;. Immaculates should get some bonus beyond them being Celestial MA though, because, if it stays the same, their thing is being able to use Celestial MA generally, at high cost, and they need some rationale to use the Dragon Styles. Immaculate Styles having separate bonuses for Immaculates and Solars seems super complicated though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:17:09-08:00","id":832157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=832154#post832154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals vs. Neil Gaiman in an all-out celestial cage match to the death! Taking all bets!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't spell normal words for a damn, much less made up words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:19:28-08:00","id":832159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=832155#post832155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immaculates should get some bonus beyond them being Celestial MA though, because, if it stays the same, their thing is being able to use Celestial MA generally, at high cost, and they need some rationale to use the Dragon Styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd assume their reason for using them will be that the Dragon styles are going to be <i>awesome</i>. They don't need extra special benefits on top of that. And from a setting perspective they'll favour Dragon styles over all the other awesome MAs because of the religious and cultural significance of those styles and the fact that all of the Immaculate sifus know and therefore teach the Dragon styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:26:50-08:00","id":832160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=832069#post832069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not so sure that would be a good thing. It's certainly possible, but then the Dragon styles would have to be balanced around the fact that you can do a fire dragon strike AND enhance it with Dragon Graced Weapon. Which basically means that the Dragon styles would all have to be really crappy. If anything I think it would be cooler if they stipulated that charms from the Immaculate styles couldn't be combined with any charms outside their style, not even other martial arts, and then let them be good and solid on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember when it was so crazy that Dragonblooded could freely use Reflexive charms without comboing. It was awesome and something no one else got! But it wasn't broken (generally) because their charmset was balanced for it. If you want a sense of how strong Dragonblooded charms will likely be, go read the martial arts charms and apply the terrestrial keyword effects. That's on-par for Terrestrials. Getting to ignore that IS a step up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:27:27-08:00","id":832162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=832159#post832159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd assume their reason for using them will be that the Dragon styles are going to be <i>awesome</i>. They don't need extra special benefits on top of that. And from a setting perspective they'll favour Dragon styles over all the other awesome MAs because of the religious and cultural significance of those styles and the fact that all of the Immaculate sifus know and therefore teach the Dragon styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, honestly even if the immaculate styles end up being weaker than other forms of MA, it'd STILL make sense for the immaculate a to be using them instead of others because their culture rams it into their head over and over that emulating the dragons is the best thing ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:31:50-08:00","id":832165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=832155#post832155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels weird to imagine Mastery effects for Immaculate Styles which Immaculates do not get. I think if you did have to include them, then they should be styled in a way that's like &quot;Well, actually the Solar's *less* in connection with the style on an elemental level, as reflected in their mechanics, yet, they just punch really hard with it anyway, because Solar essence&quot;. Immaculates should get some bonus beyond them being Celestial MA though, because, if it stays the same, their thing is being able to use Celestial MA generally, at high cost, and they need some rationale to use the Dragon Styles. Immaculate Styles having separate bonuses for Immaculates and Solars seems super complicated though.</div> </div> </div> </div>One way I see around it could be to make the process of obtaining Mastery for Dragon Blooded more complicated than the default Mastery Solars have. Maybe a Dragon Blooded only gets Mastery while using the form charm for an Immaculate style they've learned all of the charms in. This will be especially true if Dragon Blooded don't have Supernal abilities because that would mean a Dragon Blooded NPC could only get Mastery in a style long after they've spent a mortal lifetime or two being a badass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:37:34-08:00","id":832172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=832162#post832162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, honestly even if the immaculate styles end up being weaker than other forms of MA, it'd STILL make sense for the immaculate a to be using them instead of others because their culture rams it into their head over and over that emulating the dragons is the best thing ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'd want to avoid a situation in which all Immaculates study those five styles... except for every single Immaculate PC, all of whom find an excuse to use something else.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:44:33-08:00","id":832178,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm hoping about the Dragon Styles is that they either have some pretty amazing synergies or that one style can cover a hole in another, such that a master of multiple styles can pull off some pretty extreme combos and/or have answers to a great variety of fighting problems.<br /> <br /> One of the rare Immaculate Grandmasters of all 5 Dragon Styles should have a pretty complete package of combat options: Good join battle, good withering and decisive attacks, good soak and defense, good disengage and rush, and so on. I mean, we are talking what, 50 combat charms, plus whatever additional native stuff that particular Grandmaster might have (I'd expect a few Ox-Bodies at minimum). They should be an absolutely terrifying opponent.<br /> <br /> Bonus points if it is easy to transition between Forms of the 5 styles<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:54:36-08:00","id":832187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=832172#post832172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'd want to avoid a situation in which all Immaculates study those five styles... except for every single Immaculate PC, all of whom find an excuse to use something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, really? Immaculate use heretical styles now? Well, not so heretical anymore I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:59:12-08:00","id":832188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/831460-\u200ball-aboard-the-dragon-blooded-hype-train?p=832187#post832187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, really? Immaculate use heretical styles now? Well, not so heretical anymore I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what he's saying is that it is wrong headed from a design standpoint to not make the immaculate styles strong because they are <b><i>the</i></b> styles for a whole player splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T17:00:25-08:00","id":832190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Ori